      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T03:39:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The creator account does not appear to be part of the authorization behavior being tested here. It is only used to create the local test user, so using different creator accounts such as LDAP_Admin or service does not provide additional coverage for the password-change authorization.\n\nUsing service also introduces an unnecessary dependency on a pre-configured, platform-specific account, which is not available on every OpenBMC platform. As discussed in issue #2280, the test may fail before the actual password-change authorization is exercised when such a creator account is not available.\n\nCould we remove creator_type from the test matrix and use the existing ${OPENBMC_USERNAME} / ${OPENBMC_PASSWORD} Administrator credentials to create the test user? This would keep the test focused on the role of the user performing the password change and avoid depending on platform-specific creator accounts.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 874,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 874,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "dec06e6d8d18dc70ba0ea1cc6c909e1b7162643a",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c9614f8_afed4484",
        "filename": "redfish/account_service/test_ldap_configuration.robot",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 874,
